urther education. B: strong reliability, stress, technical, but poor cooperation and memory for numbers. Which is more critical? Crew cooperation is vital. Communication issues for C may be mitigated; egocentric may affect crew but positive atmosphere suggests good cooperation. Not willing to further education may affect long-term development but maybe less immediate.\n\nThus I would recommend Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 3 recommended B, Agent 1 recommended C. We can either align with Agent 1 or propose our own. Since we are agent 2, we can support Candidate C, referencing evidence: 100% reliability, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions, calm in crisis. Also note concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education, but weigh against B's uncooperative remarks.\n\nThus our vote: Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: concise, referencing prior discussion, giving evidence, concluding recommendation.\n\nProceed."}
